      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ORDER ONLINE (1) sets the standard after a BM70 second at this track, where he sat handy, travelled well and was only run down late by Bon's Your Back. He has a win and three placings from four previous starts around 1200m, has never missed a place at this venue, and the move back from Saturday company reads well for this BM64. ANKLE ROLEX (6) is the clear danger on profile, coming off a third on the quick back-up after being slow away and wide around the home turn. His track-and-distance record and strong association with Billy Cray keep him right in the race despite the rise in grade. PHYSICAL GRAFFITI (4) returns from a two-month freshening after a BM70 third and has a reliable 1200m base, including five wins around the trip. Include. CAVENDISH (2) resumes with a strong overall record and a previous win at this distance, but his final run before the break was plain, so his place claims rest on recapturing the sharper form shown when beating Limited Risk at this track.",
